}

::ENG3_U05_L07_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.W.04] Draft: This is important because it helps the reader. What is the best publication-polish move? {
~A. Keep "this" because readers can guess.#Incorrect. Publication-ready writing should not force readers to guess. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
=B. Replace "this" with the specific idea being discussed.#Correct. Naming the idea improves clarity and polish. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. Add more vague words after "important."#Incorrect. More vague wording weakens polish. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. Delete the whole paragraph without checking meaning.#Incorrect. The sentence can be improved through revision. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}
